# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated vanilla data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Block/state/registry data extracted from a local Minecraft installation by
# src/engine/blockdb_setup.c. It is derived from Mojang content, so it must
# never be committed - see docs/PARITY_BOUNDARY.md. The client regenerates it
# on launch when it is missing.
generated/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build products
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tools/bundle.py emits build/<name>.cpy, `cpyte build` emits the object files
# and dist/<name>.exe. ./build.sh and ./test.sh regenerate all of it.
build/
dist/
logs/
*.o
*.a
*.dSYM/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python tooling caches (build-time only; the shipped binary has no Python)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Note on already-tracked files: .gitignore does not untrack anything. Before
# this file existed, build/, dist/, some src/*.o and generated/blockdb.bin were
# committed. `git rm -r --cached build dist src/engine/blockdb.o src/network.o
# generated` stops tracking them while leaving the files on disk.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Embedded single-player server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# server/ holds our own FFI shim over Pumpkin (its source is MIT). Pumpkin
# itself is fetched into vendor/ by tools/pumpkin_host.sh: it is GPL-3.0, and
# its build generates Mojang-derived data. Nothing under vendor/ belongs in
# this repository. server/target/ holds the static library the client links.
vendor/
server/target/
server/Cargo.lock
